ars)","anomalies from the calendar-month normal; Sen's slope, Mann-Kendall (Yue-Wang), OLS with effective sample size (trend_stats.py)"],"synthetic":false,"caveat":"Data: MERRA-2 reanalysis, a weather model corrected by observations, about 50 km squares. The trend is a straight line through 1981–2025; it shows what changed, not why. Jan, Feb, Nov, Dec hardly change from year to year (e.g. dry season, or no snow in summer). The median-based slope (Sen) can then be pulled toward zero; compare it with the regression slope."}}